1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,729
This is a living neural circuit on a chip: rat cortical
neurons growing over sixty electrodes.

2
00:00:09,979 --> 00:00:12,018
Every dot is a spike.

3
00:00:12,268 --> 00:00:16,676
Every couple of minutes, the whole network fires at once.

4
00:00:17,236 --> 00:00:24,780
Labs summarise recordings like these with firing rates,
burst counts and synchrony, and watch them change as

5
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:25,898
cultures mature.

6
00:00:26,148 --> 00:00:28,366
These numbers describe.

7
00:00:28,616 --> 00:00:36,596
They cannot say why a network bursts, how sure we should be,
or what it would do under a change nobody has tried.

8
00:00:37,156 --> 00:00:44,594
NeuroTwin turns a recording into a mechanistic digital twin:
a simulated culture on the same chip, whose biophysical

9
00:00:44,594 --> 00:00:51,262
parameters are inferred from that recording, together with
checks that say when the twin can be trusted.

10
00:00:51,822 --> 00:00:59,994
The simulator is the chip itself: four hundred model neurons
on the same sixty-electrode layout, with synaptic

11
00:00:59,994 --> 00:01:05,418
depression, adaptation, fast and slow synaptic currents, and
noisy drive.

12
00:01:05,668 --> 00:01:10,335
A five-minute culture costs about ten seconds of one
processor core.

13
00:01:10,895 --> 00:01:17,601
We simulate tens of thousands of virtual cultures and train
a neural posterior estimator once.

14
00:01:17,851 --> 00:01:25,303
Fitting a new recording then takes a fraction of a second,
and its uncertainty is honest: ninety-percent intervals

15
00:01:25,303 --> 00:01:29,748
contain the true value eighty-six to ninety-two percent of
the time.

16
00:01:30,308 --> 00:01:34,093
Our first round failed, and the system said so.

17
00:01:34,343 --> 00:01:42,149
Three in four real recording windows lay outside anything
the simulator could produce, and the twin flagged its own

18
00:01:42,149 --> 00:01:43,642
fits as extrapolation.

19
00:01:43,892 --> 00:01:47,917
A confident wrong answer is the real danger in this field.

20
00:01:48,477 --> 00:01:51,001
The diagnosis was concrete.

21
00:01:51,251 --> 00:01:58,787
Instantaneous synapses cannot sustain a two-second burst,
and bursting cultures were rare among the simulations.

22
00:01:59,037 --> 00:02:05,960
We gave synapses realistic time courses, and concentrated
the simulations where real cultures live.

23
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:14,040
Now each twin reproduces its own recording: ninety-one
percent of its statistics fall inside the predicted range,

24
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:18,298
against fifty-two percent for the twin of a different
recording.

25
00:02:18,548 --> 00:02:26,307
And the twin still declines most recordings: twenty-two
percent of windows pass every check, and it says which.

26
00:02:26,867 --> 00:02:34,795
Across two hundred and eleven culture-days that pass every
check, the twins describe maturation in mechanistic terms.

27
00:02:35,045 --> 00:02:42,628
Within individual cultures, background drive and
excitability spread rise and adaptation decays faster, in

28
00:02:42,628 --> 00:02:46,705
two different model versions, and excitation strengthens.

29
00:02:47,265 --> 00:02:53,055
Here is one culture's twin, fitted to minutes twenty to
twenty-five of its recording.

30
00:02:53,305 --> 00:02:58,054
Like the culture, it fires large, network-wide bursts.

31
00:02:58,304 --> 00:03:04,422
Because the twin is mechanistic, we can ask it questions the
experiment never asked.

32
00:03:04,982 --> 00:03:13,019
Halve its excitation, and bursting stops in every version of
the twin, on every simulated network: a confident

33
00:03:13,019 --> 00:03:13,822
prediction.

34
00:03:14,072 --> 00:03:22,595
Halve its inhibition, and synchrony usually rises, but by
how much, and even whether, depends on what this recording

35
00:03:22,595 --> 00:03:23,771
cannot pin down.

36
00:03:24,021 --> 00:03:27,177
The twin says so, instead of guessing.

37
00:03:27,427 --> 00:03:31,316
Both are experiments a lab can run on the same chip.

38
00:03:31,876 --> 00:03:37,812
A label-free imaging module predicts nuclear and dead-cell
stains from unstained images.

39
00:03:38,062 --> 00:03:45,755
Its pixels are less faithful than the published 2018
model's, yet its nuclei counts are closer to the truth,

40
00:03:45,755 --> 00:03:52,521
within two percent on average, and their ninety-percent
intervals held in all eight test wells.

41
00:03:53,081 --> 00:03:59,985
For oriented chips built with axon diodes, the twin asks how
to read which way the axons grow.

42
00:04:00,235 --> 00:04:07,917
Five minutes of spontaneous activity give the right
direction fifty-nine percent of the time, and forty minutes

43
00:04:07,917 --> 00:04:10,962
only sixty-five, with overstated confidence.

44
00:04:11,212 --> 00:04:17,972
The design rule: probe the direction by stimulating one
chamber, rather than recording longer.

45
00:04:18,532 --> 00:04:26,689
Everything is public and runs on ordinary computers: the
data, the notebooks that reproduce every number, and an app

46
00:04:26,689 --> 00:04:29,431
that fits a twin to your own recording.

47
00:04:29,991 --> 00:04:37,093
NeuroTwin: from description to prediction for neural
organs-on-chips, with uncertainty you can check.

